window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-f05fc21d24fe24c1"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"configuration\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">配置</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>配置会影响 ChatGPT 与 Codex 开发者工具在对话、代码库和不同设备上的行为。持久上下文、配置文件、代码库指引、子智能体、外部连接，以及 Linux 和 Windows 设置共同配合，让个人与团队的工作流程保持一致。</p> <p>设置默认值、添加持久上下文，并自定义 ChatGPT 和 Codex 开发者工具的工作方式。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2645e597941a2d38\">探索自定义选项</a> <a id=\"customization\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_2\">自定义</h2> <p>调整使用体验，并在不同对话之间保留有用的上下文。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2645e597941a2d38\">自定义概览</a> — 使用指引、技能、MCP 和子智能体来自定义 ChatGPT 与 Codex。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a> — 让 ChatGPT 在不同对话之间保留有用的上下文。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\">计算机历史记录</a> — 将近期计算机活动用作上下文，并管理纳入的内容。 <a id=\"config-file\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_3\">配置文件</h2> <p>通过配置文件和变量控制模型、工具、环境与默认值。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a> — 了解配置层级并创建配置文件。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">高级配置</a> — 使用配置档案、提供商、策略和高级选项。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a> — 查找所有受支持的配置键。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-22d54b5578c4f826\">环境变量</a> — 设置会因系统和会话而变化的值。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f52101a0e13391a3\">配置示例</a> — 从完整且带注释的配置示例开始。 <a id=\"agent-configuration\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_4\">智能体配置</h2> <p>指导智能体如何协作并遵循项目指引。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md</a> — 为 Codex 提供适用于代码库的持久指令。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">子智能体</a> — 将专门任务委派给具备相应能力的智能体。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583\">速度</a> — 控制 Codex 工作的速度和深入程度。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6c7aa55b479f9cdd\">规则</a> — 定义 Codex 可以自动运行的命令。 <a id=\"extend-chatgpt-and-codex\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-codex\">扩展 ChatGPT 与 Codex</h2> <p>打包知识、连接服务并添加能力。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2c6e218368c091d9\">录制与回放</a> — 向 ChatGPT 或 Codex 展示工作流程，并将其转换为可重复使用的技能。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a> — 将 Codex 开发者工具连接到外部工具和上下文。</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"linux\">Linux</h2> <p>在受支持的 Linux 桌面环境中安装和更新 ChatGPT。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8701a8c2ceb3943c\">ChatGPT 桌面应用</a> — 在 Ubuntu、Debian、Fedora 或 Arch Linux 上安装 Linux 预览版。</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"windows\">Windows</h2> <p>在 Windows 原生环境或 WSL 中运行 Codex。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b\">ChatGPT 桌面应用</a> — 将 ChatGPT 桌面应用与 PowerShell 或 WSL 工作流程搭配使用。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2\">Windows 沙箱</a> — 使用原生文件系统和命令隔离来运行 Codex。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b77766a4300953ff\">WSL</a> — 在由 Windows 管理的 Linux 环境中使用 Codex。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"configuration\">Configuration</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Configuration shapes how ChatGPT and Codex developer tools behave across chats, repositories, and machines. Durable context, config files, repository guidance, subagents, external connections, and Linux and Windows setup work together to keep those workflows consistent for individuals and teams.</p> <p>Set defaults, add durable context, and customize how ChatGPT and Codex developer tools work.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2645e597941a2d38\">Explore customization</a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"customization\">Customization</h2> <p>Adapt the experience and carry useful context between chats.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2645e597941a2d38\">Customization overview</a> — Customize ChatGPT and Codex with guidance, skills, MCP, and subagents.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">Memories</a> — Let ChatGPT retain useful context across chats.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\">Computer History</a> — Use recent computer activity as context and manage what is included.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"config-file\">Config file</h2> <p>Control models, tools, environments, and defaults with configuration files and variables.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a> — Understand configuration layers and create a config file.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85\">Advanced config</a> — Use profiles, providers, policies, and advanced options.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Config reference</a> — Look up every supported configuration key.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-22d54b5578c4f826\">Environment variables</a> — Set values that change across systems and sessions.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f52101a0e13391a3\">Sample config</a> — Start from a complete, annotated configuration example.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"agent-configuration\">Agent configuration</h2> <p>Shape how agents collaborate and follow project guidance.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md</a> — Give Codex durable instructions for a repository.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">Subagents</a> — Delegate focused tasks to specialized agents.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583\">Speed</a> — Control how quickly and deeply Codex works.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6c7aa55b479f9cdd\">Rules</a> — Define commands Codex can run automatically.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"extend-chatgpt-and-codex\">Extend ChatGPT and Codex</h2> <p>Package knowledge, connect services, and add capabilities.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2c6e218368c091d9\">Record &amp; Replay</a> — Show ChatGPT or Codex a workflow and turn it into a reusable skill.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a> — Connect Codex developer tools to external tools and context.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"linux\">Linux</h2> <p>Install and update ChatGPT on a supported Linux desktop.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8701a8c2ceb3943c\">ChatGPT desktop app</a> — Install the Linux preview on Ubuntu, Debian, Fedora, or Arch Linux.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"windows\">Windows</h2> <p>Run Codex natively on Windows or inside WSL.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ce14d03dc374424b\">ChatGPT desktop app</a> — Use the ChatGPT desktop app with PowerShell or WSL workflows.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d86b339c4d76bce2\">Windows sandbox</a> — Run Codex with native filesystem and command isolation.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b77766a4300953ff\">WSL</a> — Use Codex in a Linux environment managed by Windows.</li> </ul>"};
